# Generated artefacts. A lock file is written by npm, never by hand, and running
# a formatter over it produces thousands of lines of diff noise on every install
# while changing nothing that matters. Worse, it makes a genuine dependency
# change impossible to spot in review.
package-lock.json
**/package-lock.json

# The API contract and the frontend types derived from it. Written by
# `npm run api:sync`, never by hand. Formatting them would be worse than noise:
# the pre-commit hook would rewrite them seconds after the generator ran, and
# CI's drift check compares the regenerated bytes against the committed ones,
# so every commit would fail on a spec nobody changed.
backend/openapi.json
frontend/src/types/api.d.ts

# The committed showcase fixture. Written by `mise run seed:fixture`, never by
# hand, and deliberately serialised one transaction per line rather than
# pretty-printed - `JSON.stringify(x, null, 2)` turns ~2,200 transactions into
# ~13,000 lines of nested indentation where a regeneration diff has to be read
# bracket by bracket. Letting Prettier reformat it expands it right back to
# that shape on the very next commit; confirmed by hand, it grew this file
# from 2,257 lines to 18,020.
backend/src/scripts/showcase/fixture.data.json

